            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Magnetic resonance imaging (MRI) is a well documented method for diagnosis of spinal disease. We discuss the changes in the number of myelographies and spinal CT examinations carried out at our department after having had our own MRI unit for two years.</AbstractText>
